selector_to_html = {"a[href=\"#pyskyfire.pump.diffuser.vane_count_conflicts\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.pump.diffuser.vane_count_conflicts\">\n<span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.pump.diffuser.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">vane_count_conflicts</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">vane_count</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">blade_count</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>Vane and blade count pairings G\u00fclich says to avoid (7.9.1 item 5, Table 10.2).</p><p>Each entry is <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">(nu2,</span> <span class=\"pre\">nu3,</span> <span class=\"pre\">m)</span></code> with <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">m</span> <span class=\"pre\">=</span> <span class=\"pre\">nu3*vane_count</span> <span class=\"pre\">-</span> <span class=\"pre\">nu2*blade_count</span></code>\nof 0 or +-1 for <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">nu</span></code> up to 3: those put a harmonic of the blade passing\non a harmonic of the vane passing, or one lobe off it, and drive pressure\npulsations. An empty tuple is a pairing he would accept.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#pyskyfire.pump.diffuser.minimum_gap_ratio\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.pump.diffuser.minimum_gap_ratio\">\n<span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.pump.diffuser.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">minimum_gap_ratio</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"keyword-only-separator o\"><abbr title=\"Keyword-only parameters separator (PEP 3102)\"><span class=\"pre\">*</span></abbr></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">nq</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">rho</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">H</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>Smallest d3/d2 G\u00fclich allows for low pressure pulsations (Table 10.2).</p><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">H</span></code> is the stage head [m] and <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">rho</span></code> its density [kg/m\u00b3]. The gap grows\nwith the energy density rho*H, which is what drives the rotor-stator\ninteraction; at the heads of a rocket pump it is well over ten percent.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"DiffuserChecks.html#pyskyfire.pump.diffuser.DiffuserChecks\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.pump.diffuser.DiffuserChecks\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.pump.diffuser.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">DiffuserChecks</span></span></dt><dd><p>The finished diffuser against G\u00fclich\u2019s criteria (7.9.1 item 10). Reported only.</p><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">gap_ratio</span></code> is d3/d2 against <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">minimum_gap_ratio</span></code> (Table 10.2).\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">inlet_width_ratio</span></code> b3/b2 should be 1.05 to 1.3. <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">throat_factor</span></code> is\nf_a3, normally 1.1 to 1.3. <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">deceleration</span></code> is c3q/c2: 0.7 to 0.85,\nhigher allowed below nq 12 to 15, and Table 10.2 asks for not much below\n0.8. <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">length_ratio</span></code> L/a3 should lie between 2.5 and 6 and\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">aspect_ratio</span></code> b3/a3 between 0.8 and 2. <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">exit_energy</span></code> is c4\u00b2/(2gH),\n0.02 to 0.04 for multistage pumps. <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">opening_angle_deg</span></code> is the equivalent\nconical half-angle (Eq. 1.45), which must stay below\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">allowed_opening_angle_deg</span></code> (Eq. 1.44) or the channel stalls.\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">vane_count_conflicts</span></code> lists each (nu2, nu3, m) with\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">|m|</span> <span class=\"pre\">=</span> <span class=\"pre\">|nu3</span> <span class=\"pre\">z_Le</span> <span class=\"pre\">-</span> <span class=\"pre\">nu2</span> <span class=\"pre\">z_La|</span></code> of 0 or 1 for nu up to 3, which G\u00fclich says\nto avoid (7.9.1 item 5, Table 10.2). <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">incidence_deg</span></code> is the vane\u2019s\nleading spiral against the approach flow, within +-3 degrees by his rule;\nit follows from the throat. <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">deflection_deg</span></code> is how far the channel\nturns the flow from throat to exit; G\u00fclich applies straight-diffuser data\nup to about 25 degrees. <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">drawn_throat_ratio</span></code> and <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">drawn_exit_ratio</span></code>\nare the throat and exit widths measured on the drawn vanes over the design\nvalues, which the camber construction meets only approximately.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#module-contents\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Module Contents<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#module-contents\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2>", "a[href=\"DiffuserResult.html#pyskyfire.pump.diffuser.DiffuserResult\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.pump.diffuser.DiffuserResult\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.pump.diffuser.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">DiffuserResult</span></span></dt><dd><p>Losses of one diffuser operating point, G\u00fclich Table 3.8 (2).</p><p>Coefficients are referred to u2\u00b2/2, as G\u00fclich writes them. <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">vaneless</span></code>\nis the wall friction between impeller and vanes (T3.8.23), <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">inlet</span></code> the\nfriction in the triangular inlet region (T3.8.18), <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">shock</span></code> the loss of\ndecelerating c2 onto the throat (the 0.3 term of T3.8.19) and <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">channel</span></code>\nthe diffusing channel, 1 - cp - 1/AR\u00b2 times the throat head. <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">mixing</span></code>\nis the channel jets filling the outlet ring: they leave through part of\nthe circumference only, the vanes\u2019 trailing edges taking the rest, and\nmixing out keeps their swirl but loses their excess radial velocity, a\nBorda-Carnot loss on that component. This is the part of G\u00fclich\u2019s overflow\nloss that belongs to the diffuser; the energy left in the mixed flow is not\ncharged, because the volute collects it and charges its own loss.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#module-pyskyfire.pump.diffuser\"]": "<h1 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">pyskyfire.pump.diffuser<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#module-pyskyfire.pump.diffuser\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h1><p>Vaned radial diffuser between an impeller and its volute.</p><p>A vaneless volute collects the impeller discharge at nearly the speed it left\nthe wheel, and it carries it round the whole circumference that way, so its\nfriction is paid at the impeller\u2019s own dynamic head. Vanes take the swirl out\nsooner. They are fixed, so they do no work: they push on the flow, remove its\nangular momentum and turn it outward, so it reaches the volute radius in a\nshort path, and the channels between them widen, so it slows by their area\nratio rather than only by the radius ratio. The volute behind then collects\nslow, low-swirl flow.</p>", "a[href=\"DiffuserOutlet.html#pyskyfire.pump.diffuser.DiffuserOutlet\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.pump.diffuser.DiffuserOutlet\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.pump.diffuser.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">DiffuserOutlet</span></span></dt><dd><p>What the diffuser hands the volute, circumferentially mixed.</p><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">cm</span></code> is the mean radial velocity over the whole outlet ring and <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">cu</span></code>\nthe mass-averaged swirl of the channel jets, both in m/s. Together with\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">radius</span></code> and <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">width</span></code> they are a volute inlet.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"DiffuserGeometry.html#pyskyfire.pump.diffuser.DiffuserGeometry\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.pump.diffuser.DiffuserGeometry\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.pump.diffuser.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">DiffuserGeometry</span></span></dt><dd><p>One vane and the walls it stands between, in the impeller\u2019s own frame.</p><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">vane</span></code> is a <code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">BladeSurface</span></code> in (x, r, theta)\nabout the shaft (+x), in the wheel\u2019s rotation sense; <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">suction</span></code> is the\nface toward the impeller and <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">pressure</span></code> the one away from it. <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">hub</span></code>\nand <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">shroud</span></code> are the (x, r) wall curves from the impeller outlet to the\ndiffuser outlet, symmetric about the impeller\u2019s outlet mid-plane at x = 0,\nwith the hub at +x as on the impeller.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#references\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">References<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#references\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2><p>G\u00fclich, J. F., <em>Centrifugal Pumps</em>, 4th ed., Springer, 2020. Tables 1.7, 3.8\n(2), 7.7 and 10.2; chapter 7.9.</p>", "a[href=\"VanedDiffuser.html#pyskyfire.pump.diffuser.VanedDiffuser\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.pump.diffuser.VanedDiffuser\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.pump.diffuser.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">VanedDiffuser</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"keyword-only-separator o\"><abbr title=\"Keyword-only parameters separator (PEP 3102)\"><span class=\"pre\">*</span></abbr></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">flow</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">d2</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">b2</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">u2</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">c2u</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">impeller_blade_count</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">n</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">H</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">nq</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">rho</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">vane_count</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">gap_ratio</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">inlet_width_ratio</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">1.15</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">outer_diameter_ratio</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">length_ratio</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">outlet_width_ratio</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">1.0</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">throat_factor</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">deceleration</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">vane_thickness_ratio</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">0.012</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">roughness</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">0.0</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">rotation</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">COUNTERCLOCKWISE</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>A vaned radial diffuser designed from the impeller it follows.</p><p>Build one with <a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#pyskyfire.pump.diffuser.VanedDiffuser.from_impeller\" title=\"pyskyfire.pump.diffuser.VanedDiffuser.from_impeller\"><code class=\"xref py py-meth docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">from_impeller()</span></code></a>. The direct constructor takes the\nimpeller outlet as numbers: <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">flow</span></code> through the impeller [m\u00b3/s], its\noutlet diameter <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">d2</span></code> and width <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">b2</span></code> [m], tip speed <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">u2</span></code> and outlet\nswirl <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">c2u</span></code> [m/s], blade count, speed <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">n</span></code> [rpm], head <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">H</span></code> [m] (the\nhead at the impeller outlet, used for the gap and exit-energy rules),\nspecific speed <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">nq</span></code>, density <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">rho</span></code> [kg/m\u00b3] and <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">rotation</span></code>.</p><p>Design inputs, with G\u00fclich\u2019s ranges:</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#functions\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Functions<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#functions\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2>", "a[href=\"#classes\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Classes<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#classes\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2>"}
skip_classes = ["headerlink", "sd-stretched-link"]

window.onload = function () {
    for (const [select, tip_html] of Object.entries(selector_to_html)) {
        const links = document.querySelectorAll(` ${select}`);
        for (const link of links) {
            if (skip_classes.some(c => link.classList.contains(c))) {
                continue;
            }

            tippy(link, {
                content: tip_html,
                allowHTML: true,
                arrow: true,
                placement: 'auto-start', maxWidth: 600, interactive: false,
                onShow(instance) {MathJax.typesetPromise([instance.popper]).then(() => {});},
            });
        };
    };
    console.log("tippy tips loaded!");
};
